 "final_text": "I give up. The theorem is false for n = 1, so it can't be proved as stated.\n\nWhen n = 1, `Klex` is `{x | x = 0 \u2228 0 < x 0}`, which is the closed half-line `[0, \u221e)` in `EuclideanSpace \u211d (Fin 1)`. That set satisfies every clause of `IsProperCone`:\n- It is closed under nonnegative scaling.\n- It is convex.\n- It is closed.\n- Its interior is nonempty.\n- It is pointed, since `x` and `-x` both in the set forces `x = 0`.\n\nSo `\u00ac IsProperCone 1 Klex` fails, even though the hypothesis `0 < n` holds. The statement would need a stronger hypothesis, such as `2 \u2264 n`, to be provable. I did not change the file.",
